# Cloudflare Workers static assets: excludes _redirects from the uploaded
# asset manifest.
#
# _redirects below is written in Netlify's syntax for that host's SPA
# fallback (`/* /index.html 200`) and Netlify still needs it exactly as
# written. But Cloudflare's asset uploader also inspects any file literally
# named `_redirects`, and under its own implicit stripping of `.html`/
# `/index` from served paths, that same rule becomes self-triggering —
# Cloudflare refuses the deploy with "Invalid _redirects configuration:
# infinite loop detected" (confirmed on a live deploy). Cloudflare doesn't
# need the file anyway: the Vite plugin already configures
# `assets.not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` in wrangler.jsonc,
# which serves the SPA fallback natively. This file only tells Cloudflare's
# uploader to skip _redirects — it has no effect on Netlify, which has no
# concept of .assetsignore.
_redirects
